      "overall_rating": 0,
      "review_title": "",
      "review_description": "I did extensive research on solar system companies and was tossing between an established company recommended by a friend and Green Incentives. Both were of the same price, but the mounting system was better for Green Incentives. I decided to give Green Incentives a go despite it being a relatively new company because Luke came across as earnest and professional and was willing to price-match to be the same as the established company.Now I regret my decision. I was not consulted regarding the orientation of my solar system. I was upset as the orientation would not be ideal for production. Upon feedback to the company, I was told by Luke that he can only go along with what his installer said when he said he consulted me (which indirectly meant that I told a lie). There was a heated exchange between us then. The installer later called me to apologise for the misunderstanding as he realised his error. Luke never apologised for not believing me. They resolved the situation by installing two more panels to make it a more viable system and I thought I could give these guys a chance since they were quick to resolve the issue.After paying up, I realised that there were holes left in my wall behind the inverter, and I was told that it was not an issue but if I am not happy, they would fix it up for me. I don't think any reasonable home owner would appreciate having holes left in their walls even if hidden by an inverter. It has been more than a month and the holes have not been fixed. Upon contacting the company, I was blamed for the delay as I was the one not returning their calls, which I never got because they were made a week after they had promised to contact me, and I was out of the country.It is not my style to put negative feedback online but I think people need to know what they are in for.",
